  <section>
    <div class=3D"section-head"><span class=3D"num">07</span><h2>Alternativ=
e palettes =E2=80=94 proposed</h2></div>
    <p class=3D"section-note">Three palettes put forward as alternatives to=
 Blue Job, each shown carrying the mark and the horizontal lockup on a ligh=
t and a dark ground from its own set. <b>Nothing here is adopted</b> =E2=80=
=94 Blue Job in =C2=A701 remains the identity. These exist to be judged aga=
inst it.</p>
    <p class=3D"section-note" style=3D"margin-top:-12px;">One note that app=
lies to all three: none of the supplied sets includes a light paper value, =
so each proposal below uses a ground derived from its own palette. That val=
ue would need to be agreed before any of these could be specified.</p>

    <div class=3D"proposal">
      <div class=3D"prop-head">
        <span class=3D"prop-name">Sea Glass</span>
        <span class=3D"prop-tag">Proposal A</span>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"prop-swatches"><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" sty=
le=3D"background:#B6B8B9;"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Mist</b>#B6B8B9</div=
></div><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" style=3D"background:#90826E;"><=
/div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Taupe</b>#90826E</div></div><div class=3D"ps"><d=
iv class=3D"bar" style=3D"background:#70B3A4;"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>=
Sage</b>#70B3A4</div></div><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" style=3D"ba=
ckground:#256464;"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Deep teal</b>#256464</div></=
div><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" style=3D"background:#142218;"></di=
v><div class=3D"lab"><b>Pine</b>#142218</div></div></div>
      <div class=3D"prop-stages">
        <div class=3D"pstage" style=3D"background:#EDEDEC;color:#142218;">
          <svg class=3D"mk" viewBox=3D"0 0 120 132" aria-hidden=3D"true" st=
yle=3D"--z1:#256464;--band:#70B3A4;--heart:#90826E;"><use href=3D"#badge-sh=
ield"></use></svg>
          <span class=3D"rule"></span>
          <span class=3D"wm"><span class=3D"w1">Coastal</span><span class=
=3D"w2" style=3D"color:#256464;">Healthcare Advocates</span></span>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"pstage" style=3D"background:#142218;color:#EDEDEC;">
          <svg class=3D"mk" viewBox=3D"0 0 120 132" aria-hidden=3D"true" st=
yle=3D"--z1:#70B3A4;--band:#256464;--heart:#90826E;"><use href=3D"#badge-sh=
ield"></use></svg>
          <span class=3D"rule"></span>
          <span class=3D"wm"><span class=3D"w1">Coastal</span><span class=
=3D"w2" style=3D"color:#70B3A4;">Healthcare Advocates</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"prop-verdict">
        <p>Cool sage over deep teal, with taupe as the one warm-leaning val=
ue. It reads calm and clinical-adjacent without the chill of a pure blue, a=
nd the pine near-black is a richer dark ground than midnight.</p>
        <p><span class=3D"cost"><b>What it costs:</b></span> taupe is a war=
m <i>neutral</i>, not a warm accent. The heart stops being the one bright p=
oint in the mark and sinks into the shield's value range =E2=80=94 exactly =
the focal point rounds 17=E2=80=9323 were spent protecting. It also moves t=
he lighthouse away from water-blue, which is most of what makes the mark re=
ad as coastal.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"proposal">
      <div class=3D"prop-head">
        <span class=3D"prop-name">Harbor Light</span>
        <span class=3D"prop-tag">Proposal B</span>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"prop-swatches"><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" sty=
le=3D"background:#DDE8ED;"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Haze</b>#DDE8ED</div=
></div><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" style=3D"background:#E6DFC9;"><=
/div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Sand</b>#E6DFC9</div></div><div class=3D"ps"><di=
v class=3D"bar" style=3D"background:#5A8AA6;"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>H=
arbor</b>#5A8AA6</div></div><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" style=3D"b=
ackground:#2D5A74;"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Deep</b>#2D5A74</div></div>=
<div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" style=3D"background:#061221;"></div><d=
iv class=3D"lab"><b>Ink</b>#061221</div></div></div>
      <div class=3D"prop-stages">
        <div class=3D"pstage" style=3D"background:#DDE8ED;color:#061221;">
          <svg class=3D"mk" viewBox=3D"0 0 120 132" aria-hidden=3D"true" st=
yle=3D"--z1:#5A8AA6;--band:#2D5A74;--heart:#061221;"><use href=3D"#badge-sh=
ield"></use></svg>
          <span class=3D"rule"></span>
          <span class=3D"wm"><span class=3D"w1">Coastal</span><span class=
=3D"w2" style=3D"color:#2D5A74;">Healthcare Advocates</span></span>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"pstage" style=3D"background:#061221;color:#DDE8ED;">
          <svg class=3D"mk" viewBox=3D"0 0 120 132" aria-hidden=3D"true" st=
yle=3D"--z1:#5A8AA6;--band:#2D5A74;--heart:#DDE8ED;"><use href=3D"#badge-sh=
ield"></use></svg>
          <span class=3D"rule"></span>
          <span class=3D"wm"><span class=3D"w1">Coastal</span><span class=
=3D"w2" style=3D"color:#5A8AA6;">Healthcare Advocates</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"prop-verdict">
        <p>The nearest relative to Blue Job =E2=80=94 same blue family, low=
er saturation, with sand as a warm paper option. This is what the current i=
dentity would look like if it were dialled down and aged twenty years: quie=
ter, more traditional, more established.</p>
        <p><b>Heart in Ink <code>#061221</code>.</b> This solves the contra=
st problem the sand heart had =E2=80=94 ink against the pale haze ground is=
 the strongest value jump available in the set, and the heart reads cleanly=
 at small sizes again. On the dark ground ink <i>is</i> the ground, so the =
mapping inverts and the heart takes Haze <code>#DDE8ED</code>; the stripe s=
tays Deep in both modes.</p>
        <p><span class=3D"cost"><b>What it costs:</b></span> the heart beco=
mes a <i>dark</i> focal point rather than a <i>warm</i> one. That is a legi=
timate direction =E2=80=94 it is what the One colour treatment already does=
 =E2=80=94 but it changes what the mark means: instead of a warm light held=
 inside a cool shield, you get a tonal mark where the heart reads as weight=
 rather than heat. Sand then has no job left in the palette except as paper=
.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class=3D"proposal">
      <div class=3D"prop-head">
        <span class=3D"prop-name">Tidewater</span>
        <span class=3D"prop-tag best">Proposal C =C2=B7 recommended</span>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"prop-swatches"><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" sty=
le=3D"background:#508594;"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Tide</b>#508594</div=
></div><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" style=3D"background:#8F8D8E;"><=
/div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Stone</b>#8F8D8E</div></div><div class=3D"ps"><d=
iv class=3D"bar" style=3D"background:#BD674A;"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>=
Terracotta</b>#BD674A</div></div><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" style=
=3D"background:#2D5966;"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Deep tide</b>#2D5966</=
div></div><div class=3D"ps"><div class=3D"bar" style=3D"background:#1B3923;=
"></div><div class=3D"lab"><b>Forest</b>#1B3923</div></div></div>
      <div class=3D"prop-stages">
        <div class=3D"pstage" style=3D"background:#F0EEEC;color:#1B3923;">
          <svg class=3D"mk" viewBox=3D"0 0 120 132" aria-hidden=3D"true" st=
yle=3D"--z1:#508594;--band:#2D5966;--heart:#BD674A;"><use href=3D"#badge-sh=
ield"></use></svg>
          <span class=3D"rule"></span>
          <span class=3D"wm"><span class=3D"w1">Coastal</span><span class=
=3D"w2" style=3D"color:#2D5966;">Healthcare Advocates</span></span>
        </div>
        <div class=3D"pstage" style=3D"background:#1B3923;color:#F0EEEC;">
          <svg class=3D"mk" viewBox=3D"0 0 120 132" aria-hidden=3D"true" st=
yle=3D"--z1:#508594;--band:#2D5966;--heart:#BD674A;"><use href=3D"#badge-sh=
ield"></use></svg>
          <span class=3D"rule"></span>
          <span class=3D"wm"><span class=3D"w1">Coastal</span><span class=
=3D"w2" style=3D"color:#508594;">Healthcare Advocates</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class=3D"prop-verdict">
        <p>The only one of the three that keeps the mark's structure intact=
. Terracotta <code>#BD674A</code> does precisely the job Coral does now =E2=
=80=94 the heart stays the single warm point in a cool mark =E2=80=94 and t=
he tide/deep-tide pair gives the shield and its stripe two distinct values =
in both modes without needing the light/dark token split. Forest green is a=
 dark ground that isn't another navy.</p>
        <p><span class=3D"cost"><b>What it costs:</b></span> terracotta is =
muted where coral is bright, so the heart carries less urgency at favicon s=
ize; and the forest ground pulls the brand toward land where the lighthouse=
 wants water. Both are liveable. <b>If the palette is genuinely in play, th=
is is the one to develop.</b></p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class=3D"flag">
      <div class=3D"mark">=E2=86=B3</div>
      <div>
        <p><b>The test any replacement has to pass.</b> The mark is built a=
round one warm point inside a cool shield =E2=80=94 that is the whole reaso=
n the heart reads before anything else does, at every size down to a favico=
n. Sea Glass fails it: taupe is a neutral, and substituting one turns the h=
eart into a hole. Harbor Light with an ink heart passes on <i>contrast</i> =
but not on <i>warmth</i> =E2=80=94 the heart is legible, but the mark becom=
es tonal rather than warm-point-in-cool-shield. Tidewater is the only one t=
hat passes outright, because terracotta is a real accent doing Coral's job.=
</p>
        <p>If the intent is a warmer or more muted brand rather than a diff=
erent one, the cheaper move is to keep Blue Job's structure and shift only =
its two neutrals =E2=80=94 Paper and Midnight =E2=80=94 toward the sand and=
 pine tones above, leaving Sky and Coral to do the work they already do.</p=
>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

